<Folder><name>Lost capitals</name>
<Placemark><name>H6 Opis (Upi), and possibly Akshak, at Tulul al-Mujaili' on a relict Diyala levee</name><styleUrl>#tA</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Opis was a major Tigris-Diyala city of Babylonian and Persian times. The DEM puts the proposed mound on a NNW-SSE relict levee 15 km NE of Ctesiphon, which splits at a distributary node 6.5 km SSW. The channel link is new; the identification is published. (Location rounded to about 10 km in the public copy.)<br/>PROPOSED | radius 10 km]]></description><LookAt><longitude>44.7</longitude><latitude>33.2</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><range>40000.0</range><tilt>30</tilt><heading>0</heading></LookAt><Point><coordinates>44.7,33.2,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
