<Folder><name>Lost cities</name>
<Placemark><name>B1 Akkad (Agade): relict-Tigris / paleo-Adhaim junction</name><styleUrl>#tB</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Akkad is the only Mesopotamian imperial capital never found. A DEM-traced relict Tigris belt splits from today's river 15 km from where the Adhaim reaches the floodplain, which joins Ziegler's confluence idea to Kawakami's ancient-riverbed idea.<br/>PARTLY-KNOWN | radius 8 km]]></description><LookAt><longitude>44.23</longitude><latitude>33.97</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><range>25000.0</range><tilt>30</tilt><heading>0</heading></LookAt><Point><coordinates>44.23,33.97,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
