<Placemark><name>B5 al-Ghaba, the royal town of ancient Ghana</name><styleUrl>#tB</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[al-Bakri (1068) puts the king's town 6 miles from the Muslim town (Koumbi Saleh). That distance meets a low plain with seasonal ponds north-west to north of Koumbi Saleh, and two unexplained 'built-up' land-cover pixels.<br/>NOVEL-SYNTHESIS | radius 7 km]]></description><LookAt><longitude>-8.017</longitude><latitude>15.846</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><range>25000.0</range><tilt>30</tilt><heading>0</heading></LookAt><Point><coordinates>-8.017,15.846,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
