<Folder><name>Lost road stations</name>
<Placemark><name>H7 Aratu, a lost Roman road station = the fort at Zawiyet el-Agdab (Egypt)</name><styleUrl>#tB</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[Aratu is on the Tabula Peutingeriana but unlocated in the Barrington Atlas. Its road distances (Catabathmus 28, Nesus 26 Roman miles) put the distance-only point in the sea, so the station must lie inland. The only recorded Roman fort within 9 km of the inland solution fits the distances to within 6%.<br/>NOVEL-SYNTHESIS | radius 3 km]]></description><LookAt><longitude>25.5039</longitude><latitude>31.3906</latitude><altitude>0</altitude><range>8000.0</range><tilt>30</tilt><heading>0</heading></LookAt><Point><coordinates>25.5039,31.3906,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
